Package: cuvis.r
Title: Interface to the Cubert 'CUVIS' Hyperspectral Imaging SDK
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: person("R.", "Heller", email = "raban.heller@uni-ulm.de",
    role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-8006-9742"))
Description: Provides an interface to the Cubert 'CUVIS' C software
    development kit (SDK) for reading, processing and exporting hyperspectral
    imaging data recorded with Cubert snapshot cameras. It supports loading
    proprietary '.cu3s' session files, applying the full calibration pipeline
    (dark subtraction, white reference normalization, spectral radiance,
    reflectance) and exporting to standard formats ('ENVI', 'TIFF'). The
    interface mirrors the API of 'cuvis.python'
    <https://github.com/cubert-hyperspectral/cuvis.python>. The 'CUVIS' SDK
    is not distributed with this package and must be installed separately;
    without it the package installs in a stub mode in which
    cuvis_available() returns FALSE and SDK operations are unavailable.
License: Apache License (>= 2)
URL: https://github.com/cttir/cuvis.r, https://cttir.github.io/cuvis.r/
